@startuml ELSTER_AsIs_FirstTimeLogin

title As-Is: First-Time Login to ELSTER using Certificate File

|Taxpayer|
start
:Navigate to elster.de and
select "create an account";

if (Registration for?) then ([Private individual])
:Enter Identification Number,
Date of Birth, Email, Username;
else ([Organization])
:Enter Federal State, Tax Number,
Contact person details, Username;
endif

repeat
    :Submit personal details;
    |ELSTER Portal|
repeat while (Submitted data valid?) is ([no]) not ([yes])

:Send verification email;

|Async Delivery Channels \nEmail System and Postal Service|
:Deliver verification email;

|Taxpayer|
:Enter 6-digit verification code
from email;

|ELSTER Portal|
:Prompt for identification method;

|Taxpayer|
if (Identity verification method?) then ([Online Identity Verification])
if (Online-ID option?) then ([Online ID function])
:Perform online identity check
using eID + 6-digit Pin + AusweisApp;
|Online identification Provider \nAusweisApp, Nect Wallet-App|
:Verify identity using eID function
and send Auth Token to Portal;
else ([Nect Wallet app])
|Taxpayer|
:Perform online identity check
using ID Card + Nect Wallet app;
|Online identification Provider \nAusweisApp, Nect Wallet-App|
:Verify identity using selfie video & audio
and send Auth Token to Portal;
endif
|ELSTER Portal|
:Receive and validate
Auth Token;
else ([Identity verification by mail])
|ELSTER Portal|
:Generate Activation ID
and Activation Code;
fork
    :Send Activation ID
    via email;
    |Async Delivery Channels \nEmail System and Postal Service|
    :Deliver email with Activation ID
    and activation link;
fork again
    |ELSTER Portal|
    :Send Activation Code
    via postal letter;
    |Async Delivery Channels \nEmail System and Postal Service|
    :Deliver letter with
    Activation Code
    (5-10 working days);
end fork

|Taxpayer|
:Open verification link from email
and enter Activation ID & Activation Code;

|ELSTER Portal|
if (Activation data valid?) then ([no])
|Taxpayer|
:Retry or request
new activation;
end
else ([yes])
endif
endif

|ELSTER Portal|
:Prompt to set up
secure login method;

|Taxpayer|
:Select "Other Login options"
-> "Certificate file";
:Enter certificate file name
and password;

|ELSTER Portal|
:Generate RSA key pair
and create .pfx file;

#LightBlue:<<pfx file>>
Certificate file (.pfx)
[created];

|Taxpayer|
:Download .pfx file
to local PC;

#LightBlue:<<pfx file>>
Certificate file (.pfx)
[stored locally];

note right
  Do NOT open or
  import the .pfx file
  on the PC
end note

:Initiate first-time login
with certificate file;

repeat
    :Browse and select
    .pfx file and enter password;
    |ELSTER Portal|
    :Validate certificate
    and password;
    if (Certificate valid\n& password correct?) then ([yes])
    |ELSTER Portal|
    stop
    else ([no])
    |Taxpayer|

    endif
    backward :Retry to login;
repeat while (Abort login attempt?) is ([no]) not ([yes])
end



legend bottom
|= Notation |= UML 2.5 element |= Meaning |
| Filled circle | Initial node | Start of the activity flow |
| Rounded rectangle | Action | An executable step within the activity |
| Diamond (1 in / n out) | Decision node | Conditional branching on guard `[condition]` |
| Diamond (n in / 1 out) | Merge node | Reconvergence of alternative branches |
| Solid bar (1 in / n out) | Fork flow | Splitting into / synchronising parallel flows |
| Solid bar (n in / 1 out) | Join flow | Synchronizing parallel flows back into one |
| Rectangle «pfx file» | Object node | A business artifact passed between actions (the .pfx file) |
| Vertical partitions | Activity partitions (swimlanes) | Allocation of actions to responsible actors |
| Filled circle in ring | Activity final node | Termination of the entire activity (success) |
| Circle with cross | Flow final node | Termination of a single flow only (failure branch) |
----
Figure 1: As-Is UML Activity Diagram — First-Time Login to ELSTER using the Certificate File
(own illustration, based on ELSTER 2026)
endlegend

@enduml